{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26811 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Hirsutene appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets, all of which are expressed in LoVo cells. The evidence suggests that Hirsutene acts as a target for multiple compounds, which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This indicates a potential mechanism where Hirsutene may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through the modulation of its downstream targets. The presence of multiple distinct compounds that share a common target, LoVo, suggests that Hirsutene may be involved in a broader regulatory network that affects the function of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Hirsutene could modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through the regulation of its target genes, potentially influencing cellular processes such as gene expression and chromatin modification.",
